IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `qld-interpretation-time`
IMPORT `qld-part05-commencement`
IMPORT `qld-part06-amendment-and-repeal`
IMPORT `qld-part10-service-of-documents`
IMPORT `qld-part12a-forms`
IMPORT `qld-part12b-fee-units`
IMPORT `qld-part13-miscellaneous`
IMPORT `qld-schedule1-terms`
IMPORT `qld-seat`

-- Worked cases for qld-seat.l4: at least one case for every question, and cases outside the encoding (NOTHING) asserted.
-- Every expected value below was worked out by hand from the text of the Act, as cited, before the file was run.
-- The weekday of each date used as a last day was read from a calendar.

§ `Cases for the seat: a person who has a time to meet`

§§ `Fixtures`

GIVETH A LIST OF DATE
`no dates` MEANS EMPTY

GIVETH A LIST OF DATE
`only Monday 2 February 2026` MEANS LIST (Date 2 2 2026)

GIVETH A LIST OF DATE
`Saturday 31 January and Sunday 1 February 2026` MEANS LIST (Date 31 1 2026), (Date 1 2 2026)

§§ `When a law takes effect, and when it stops`

-- s 15A: an Act commences on the date of assent except so far as the Act otherwise expressly provides.
-- SAYS An Act that does not expressly provide otherwise commences on the date of assent; if it does expressly provide otherwise, s 15A does not say when it commences (s 15A).
#ASSERT `On which day does an Act take effect if it says nothing different about its start` (Date 5 4 1995) FALSE EQUALS JUST (Date 5 4 1995)
#ASSERT `On which day does an Act take effect if it says nothing different about its start` (Date 5 4 1995) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 15D(2): a day fixed before the notification day is still the day fixed, but the Act commences on the notification day.
#ASSERT `On which day does an Act take effect when its start is fixed by proclamation` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 10 3 2026) EQUALS Date 10 3 2026
#ASSERT `On which day does an Act take effect when its start is fixed by proclamation` (Date 20 3 2026) (Date 10 3 2026) EQUALS Date 20 3 2026
#ASSERT `On which day does an Act take effect when its start is fixed by proclamation` (Date 10 3 2026) (Date 10 3 2026) EQUALS Date 10 3 2026

-- s 15DA and its Example: assent on 5 April 1995, not commenced by 5 April 1996, so it commences on 6 April 1996.
#ASSERT `On which day does an Act whose start was left to a proclamation start by itself` (Date 5 4 1995) FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST (Date 6 4 1996)
-- s 15DA(3): a regulation made within the year extends the period to not more than 2 years of the assent day: to 5 April 1997, so 6 April 1997.
#ASSERT `On which day does an Act whose start was left to a proclamation start by itself` (Date 5 4 1995) FALSE 24 EQUALS JUST (Date 6 4 1997)
-- More than 2 years is outside s 15DA(3): the Act does not say.
#ASSERT `On which day does an Act whose start was left to a proclamation start by itself` (Date 5 4 1995) FALSE 25 EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 15DA(5)(a): only a postponed law enacted after 31 December 1994.
#ASSERT `On which day does an Act whose start was left to a proclamation start by itself` (Date 31 12 1994) FALSE 0 EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 15DA(5)(b): unless an Act expressly states that the section does not apply.
#ASSERT `On which day does an Act whose start was left to a proclamation start by itself` (Date 5 4 1995) TRUE 0 EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 17(3): a thing necessary under s 17(3) takes effect on the day it is made, or on the later day at which it is expressed to take effect.
-- SAYS An instrument made before its enabling law commences takes effect on the day it is made, or on the later day at which it is expressed to take effect, if it is necessary to enable the power to be exercised or brought into effect (s 17(3)).
#ASSERT `On which day does an instrument or appointment made before its enabling law starts take effect` FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 7 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2020) EQUALS Date 1 3 2026
#ASSERT `On which day does an instrument or appointment made before its enabling law starts take effect` FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 7 2026) TRUE (Date 15 3 2026) EQUALS Date 15 3 2026
-- s 17(4): an appointment, or an instrument not necessary under s 17(3), takes effect on the commencement of the enabling provision, or the later day expressed.
#ASSERT `On which day does an instrument or appointment made before its enabling law starts take effect` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 7 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2020) EQUALS Date 1 7 2026
#ASSERT `On which day does an instrument or appointment made before its enabling law starts take effect` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 7 2026) TRUE (Date 1 9 2026) EQUALS Date 1 9 2026

-- s 15B: a provision that commences on 12 April 1995 commences at the beginning of that day.
-- SAYS A provision that commences on a day is in force from the beginning of that day, not from its end (s 15B).
#ASSERT `Is a law already in force at the beginning of a given day` (Date 12 4 1995) (Date 12 4 1995)
#ASSERT `Is a law already in force at the beginning of a given day` (Date 12 4 1995) (Date 13 4 1995)
#ASSERT NOT `Is a law already in force at the beginning of a given day` (Date 12 4 1995) (Date 11 4 1995)

-- s 18: a provision that expires on 30 June 2026 has effect until the end of that day.
-- SAYS A provision that expires on a day, or that remains in force until a day, has effect until the end of that day (s 18).
#ASSERT `Is a law still in force at the beginning of a given day if it expires on a day` (Date 30 6 2026) (Date 30 6 2026)
#ASSERT `Is a law still in force at the beginning of a given day if it expires on a day` (Date 30 6 2026) (Date 29 6 2026)
#ASSERT NOT `Is a law still in force at the beginning of a given day if it expires on a day` (Date 30 6 2026) (Date 1 7 2026)

-- s 20(2) and (4): a repeal or amendment does not revive or affect a right, privilege or liability acquired, accrued or incurred under the Act.
-- For any other thing the two subsections do not say.
#ASSERT `Does the repeal of an Act take away a right or liability I acquired under it` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does the repeal of an Act take away a right or liability I acquired under it` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 20(3): an investigation, proceeding or remedy relating to a right, privilege, liability or penalty may be started, continued or completed, the right enforced or the penalty imposed.
#ASSERT `May I take a step about a right or penalty under a repealed Act as if it had not been repealed` TRUE `the investigation, proceeding or remedy is started` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `May I take a step about a right or penalty under a repealed Act as if it had not been repealed` TRUE `the penalty is imposed` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A step that is not one of those the subsection names, or a thing not within s 20(2)(c) or (d): the subsection does not say.
#ASSERT `May I take a step about a right or penalty under a repealed Act as if it had not been repealed` TRUE `any other step` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `May I take a step about a right or penalty under a repealed Act as if it had not been repealed` FALSE `the investigation, proceeding or remedy is started` EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Counting my period: the six worked cases`

-- Each case is asked twice: for a thing other than filing or registering a document, with no holiday, so a Saturday or Sunday is an excluded day (s 38(5)(b), Schedule 1 "business day");
-- and for filing or registering a document at an office that is closed on no listed day (s 38(5)(a)), so no day is excluded.

-- Thirty days from 1 January 2026: 1 January is excluded, so day 30 is 31 January 2026, a Saturday.
-- SAYS A period of days beginning on a given day excludes that day and includes the last day, so thirty days from 1 January 2026 end on 31 January 2026 (s 38(1)).
#ASSERT `On which day does my period of days end` (Date 1 1 2026) 30 FALSE `no dates` `no dates` EQUALS JUST (Date 2 2 2026)
#ASSERT `On which day does my period of days end` (Date 1 1 2026) 30 TRUE `no dates` `no dates` EQUALS JUST (Date 31 1 2026)
-- Filing at an office closed on Saturday 31 January and Sunday 1 February 2026: the next later day that is not closed is Monday 2 February.
#ASSERT `On which day does my period of days end` (Date 1 1 2026) 30 TRUE `Saturday 31 January and Sunday 1 February 2026` `no dates` EQUALS JUST (Date 2 2 2026)
-- Monday 2 February 2026 is also a holiday of the place: the next later day that is not an excluded day is Tuesday 3 February.
#ASSERT `On which day does my period of days end` (Date 1 1 2026) 30 FALSE `no dates` `only Monday 2 February 2026` EQUALS JUST (Date 3 2 2026)
-- A period that gives no days is not a period the Act counts.
#ASSERT `On which day does my period of days end` (Date 1 1 2026) 0 FALSE `no dates` `no dates` EQUALS NOTHING

-- Two months from 31 December 2025: January (1 to 31 January), then February (1 to 28 February 2026, a Saturday).
-- SAYS Two months from 31 December 2025 end on 28 February 2026, the last day of the second calendar month, which begins on the day after the given day (Schedule 1 "calendar month", s 38(1)).
#ASSERT `On which day does my period of months end` (Date 31 12 2025) 2 FALSE `no dates` `no dates` EQUALS JUST (Date 2 3 2026)
#ASSERT `On which day does my period of months end` (Date 31 12 2025) 2 TRUE `no dates` `no dates` EQUALS JUST (Date 28 2 2026)
-- One month from 31 January 2024: the month begins on 1 February and ends immediately before 1 March: 29 February 2024, a Thursday.
#ASSERT `On which day does my period of months end` (Date 31 1 2024) 1 FALSE `no dates` `no dates` EQUALS JUST (Date 29 2 2024)
#ASSERT `On which day does my period of months end` (Date 31 1 2024) 1 TRUE `no dates` `no dates` EQUALS JUST (Date 29 2 2024)
-- One month from 30 January 2023: the month begins on 31 January; there is no 31 February, so it ends at the end of February: 28 February 2023, a Tuesday.
#ASSERT `On which day does my period of months end` (Date 30 1 2023) 1 FALSE `no dates` `no dates` EQUALS JUST (Date 28 2 2023)

-- Three years from 16 July 2025: 36 calendar months beginning on 17 July 2025, ending 16 July 2028, a Sunday.
#ASSERT `On which day does my period of years end` (Date 16 7 2025) 3 FALSE `no dates` `no dates` EQUALS JUST (Date 17 7 2028)
#ASSERT `On which day does my period of years end` (Date 16 7 2025) 3 TRUE `no dates` `no dates` EQUALS JUST (Date 16 7 2028)
-- Five years from 15 January 2025: 60 calendar months beginning on 16 January 2025, ending 15 January 2030, a Tuesday.
#ASSERT `On which day does my period of years end` (Date 15 1 2025) 5 FALSE `no dates` `no dates` EQUALS JUST (Date 15 1 2030)
-- Five years from 1 September 2025: ending 1 September 2030, a Sunday, so Monday 2 September 2030 for a thing other than filing.
#ASSERT `On which day does my period of years end` (Date 1 9 2025) 5 FALSE `no dates` `no dates` EQUALS JUST (Date 2 9 2030)
#ASSERT `On which day does my period of years end` (Date 1 9 2025) 5 TRUE `no dates` `no dates` EQUALS JUST (Date 1 9 2030)
-- One year from 29 February 2024: 12 calendar months beginning on 1 March 2024, ending 28 February 2025, a Friday.
#ASSERT `On which day does my period of years end` (Date 29 2 2024) 1 FALSE `no dates` `no dates` EQUALS JUST (Date 28 2 2025)

§§ `Counting my period: clear days, which days count, and counting back`

-- s 38(1)(a): fourteen clear days from 1 January 2026 exclude 1 January and the day the thing is done: 2 to 15 January are the clear days, so 16 January is the earliest.
#ASSERT `On which day is the earliest I can act after a number of clear days` (Date 1 1 2026) 14 EQUALS JUST (Date 16 1 2026)
#ASSERT `On which day is the earliest I can act after a number of clear days` (Date 1 1 2026) 0 EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 38(1): the day, act or event from which the period runs is excluded; the day after it is the first day counted.
#ASSERT NOT `Does a day count in my period if the period begins on a given day` (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 1 2026)
#ASSERT `Does a day count in my period if the period begins on a given day` (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 2 1 2026)
#ASSERT NOT `Does a day count in my period if the period begins on a given day` (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 31 12 2025)

-- s 38(1)(a) and (b): the day on which the thing is to be done is not counted for clear days or at least a number of days; in any other case it is.
#ASSERT NOT `Is the day on which I must act counted in my period` TRUE
#ASSERT `Is the day on which I must act counted in my period` FALSE

-- s 38(1) and (3): seven days back from Sunday 15 March 2026 is Sunday 8 March; a thing other than filing moves back to the next earlier day that is not excluded: Friday 6 March.
#ASSERT `On which day is the earliest I may act if I must act a number of days before a given day` (Date 15 3 2026) 7 FALSE `no dates` `no dates` EQUALS JUST (Date 6 3 2026)
-- For filing at an office closed on no listed day, no day is excluded.
#ASSERT `On which day is the earliest I may act if I must act a number of days before a given day` (Date 15 3 2026) 7 TRUE `no dates` `no dates` EQUALS JUST (Date 8 3 2026)
-- Fourteen days back from Friday 20 March 2026 is Friday 6 March 2026, which is not excluded.
#ASSERT `On which day is the earliest I may act if I must act a number of days before a given day` (Date 20 3 2026) 14 FALSE `no dates` `no dates` EQUALS JUST (Date 6 3 2026)
#ASSERT `On which day is the earliest I may act if I must act a number of days before a given day` (Date 20 3 2026) 0 FALSE `no dates` `no dates` EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 38(5): for filing or registering a document an excluded day is a day on which the office is closed; otherwise it is a day that is not a business day.
-- SAYS For a thing other than filing or registering a document, an excluded day is a day that is not a business day, that is a Saturday, a Sunday or a public holiday, special holiday or bank holiday in the place (s 38(5)(b), Schedule 1 "business day").
#ASSERT `Is a given day a day that does not count when my last day falls on it` (Date 31 1 2026) FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Is a given day a day that does not count when my last day falls on it` (Date 2 2 2026) FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `Is a given day a day that does not count when my last day falls on it` (Date 2 2 2026) FALSE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `Is a given day a day that does not count when my last day falls on it` (Date 2 2 2026) TRUE TRUE FALSE
-- Filing or registering: the office open on a Saturday is not an excluded day, since the paragraph looks only at whether the office is closed.
#ASSERT NOT `Is a given day a day that does not count when my last day falls on it` (Date 31 1 2026) TRUE FALSE FALSE

-- s 38(4): if no time is provided or allowed, the thing is to be done as soon as possible, and as often as the occasion happens.
#ASSERT `Must I act as soon as possible because no time is set` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Must I act as soon as possible because no time is set` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Age and adulthood`

-- s 38A: a person is an age in years at the beginning of the person's birthday for the age.
-- Born 15 June 2000: aged 18 at the beginning of 15 June 2018, still 17 on 14 June 2018; no age before the birth.
#ASSERT `How old am I on a given day` (Date 15 6 2000) (Date 15 6 2018) EQUALS JUST 18
#ASSERT `How old am I on a given day` (Date 15 6 2000) (Date 14 6 2018) EQUALS JUST 17
#ASSERT `How old am I on a given day` (Date 15 6 2000) (Date 1 1 1999) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Born 29 February 2000: in a year with a 29 February the birthday is that day; in a year without one the Act does not say whether 28 February is the birthday.
#ASSERT `How old am I on a given day` (Date 29 2 2000) (Date 29 2 2024) EQUALS JUST 24
#ASSERT `How old am I on a given day` (Date 29 2 2000) (Date 28 2 2024) EQUALS JUST 23
#ASSERT `How old am I on a given day` (Date 29 2 2000) (Date 28 2 2023) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `How old am I on a given day` (Date 29 2 2000) (Date 1 3 2023) EQUALS JUST 23

-- Schedule 1: an adult is an individual who is 18 or more.
#ASSERT `Am I an adult on a given day` (Date 15 6 2000) (Date 15 6 2018) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I an adult on a given day` (Date 15 6 2000) (Date 14 6 2018) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I an adult on a given day` (Date 15 6 2000) (Date 15 6 2018) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I an adult on a given day` (Date 15 6 2000) (Date 1 1 1999) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Serving documents, and when a posted letter counts`

-- s 39(1): on an individual, by delivering personally, by leaving at the last known address, or by sending by post to it.
-- SAYS A document that an Act requires or permits to be served on an individual may be served by delivering it personally, by leaving it at, or by sending it by post to, the last known address of residence or business (s 39(1)).
#ASSERT `May a document be served on a person in a given way` TRUE `an individual` `by delivering it to the person personally` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `May a document be served on a person in a given way` TRUE `a body corporate` `by leaving it at the head office, a registered office or a principal office of the body corporate` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A way the subsection does not list for that person, or no Act that requires or permits the service: the subsection does not say.
#ASSERT `May a document be served on a person in a given way` TRUE `an individual` `in any other way` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `May a document be served on a person in a given way` TRUE `an individual` `by leaving it at the head office, a registered office or a principal office of the body corporate` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `May a document be served on a person in a given way` FALSE `an individual` `by delivering it to the person personally` EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 39A(1)(a): service by post may be effected by properly addressing, prepaying and posting the document as a letter.
#ASSERT `Is service by post effected by posting my document as a letter` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is service by post effected by posting my document as a letter` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 39A(1)(b): service is taken to have been effected when the letter would be delivered in the ordinary course of post, unless the contrary is proved.
-- Delivered at 9 am (32400 seconds) on 10 March 2026: effected in the course of 10 March, so by the end of 10 March.
#ASSERT `Is my posted letter taken to have been served by the end of my last day` (Date 10 3 2026) 32400 FALSE (Date 10 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Delivered on 11 March 2026: after the end of 10 March.
#ASSERT `Is my posted letter taken to have been served by the end of my last day` (Date 11 3 2026) 32400 FALSE (Date 10 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Delivered on 9 March 2026: before the end of 10 March.
#ASSERT `Is my posted letter taken to have been served by the end of my last day` (Date 9 3 2026) 32400 FALSE (Date 10 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- When the contrary is proved the Act gives no time.
#ASSERT `Is my posted letter taken to have been served by the end of my last day` (Date 10 3 2026) 32400 TRUE (Date 10 3 2026) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Forms, verification and fee units`

-- s 48A(1): strict compliance with a prescribed or approved form is not necessary, and substantial compliance is sufficient.
#ASSERT `Is it enough that my form substantially complies with the prescribed form` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is it enough that my form substantially complies with the prescribed form` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Is it enough that my form substantially complies with the prescribed form` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 48A(2): the form is not properly completed unless the requirement is complied with.
#ASSERT `Is my form properly completed if the form's requirement is not complied with` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is my form properly completed if the form's requirement is not complied with` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Is my form properly completed if the form's requirement is not complied with` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 49: if an Act requires verification in a specified way, the purpose is not fulfilled unless the requirement is satisfied.
#ASSERT `Is the purpose fulfilled if the verification the Act requires is not satisfied` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is the purpose fulfilled if the verification the Act requires is not satisfied` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Is the purpose fulfilled if the verification the Act requires is not satisfied` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 48B(4): the value of a fee unit is the amount prescribed, or $1 if none is prescribed.
-- s 48C(3): the amount is the value times the number of fee units, rounded to the nearest cent, one-half upwards.
-- 10 fee units at a prescribed $1.50 is $15.
#ASSERT `How many dollars is a fee expressed in fee units` 10 TRUE 1.5 FALSE EQUALS JUST 15
-- 10 fee units, no value prescribed: $1 each, so $10.
#ASSERT `How many dollars is a fee expressed in fee units` 10 FALSE 0 FALSE EQUALS JUST 10
-- 3 fee units at $1.234 is $3.702, which rounds to $3.70.
#ASSERT `How many dollars is a fee expressed in fee units` 3 TRUE 1.234 FALSE EQUALS JUST 3.7
-- One-half cent rounds upwards: 1 fee unit at $0.005 is $0.01.
#ASSERT `How many dollars is a fee expressed in fee units` 1 TRUE 0.005 FALSE EQUALS JUST 0.01
-- An Act that provides its own way of rounding: this question does not cover it.
#ASSERT `How many dollars is a fee expressed in fee units` 3 TRUE 1.234 TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
